ou how how  clean this technique is and  you know you get a lot more lifespan out  of your column and so on and so forth  uh one of the biggest disadvantages  really to headspace is that  method development is mind-numbingly  painful  because you have to wait for the vial to  heat up so say  you have a 15-minute incubation time  then you're waiting for that 15 minutes  plus another 15-minute run time  so you're looking at 32 minutes plus  from injection to injection but once the  methods developed you really only pay  that price  first you know with the first sample  most modern headspace systems  uh have staged um  incubation so that's not as much as a  concern as it  was years ago  once you've decided on your injection  technique you want to look at  whether you're going to use a split so  split flipless injections  i think basically all modern gc's for  the most part  um have split surface injection ports  so a split basically allows  for you to only inject a fraction of the  effluent into the actual column  and the the remainder is sort of swept  off  and vented so this is useful  primarily in uh liquid injection  so there's you know you don't want to  overload the column  so depending on what you're doing you  can go anywhere from like a ten to one  split to 100 to one split  uh depends on your sample prep how  concentrated your injection is and so on  and so forth  um footless injections primarily used  with headspace but you can do a split  if you want typically what i do is i'll  adjust the actual injection time on the  headspace unit  setting splits and uh you know basically  when you run into  this injection um the uh this football  just remains closed  so the next phase of this is sorting out  your chromatography  and the separation of terpenes  can be kind of difficult and the primary  reason for that  is that because they are these sort of  five units or  sorry five carbon repeating units of  isoprene um they are structurally very  similar  and uh you k